<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sūbŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>an awl</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 3,
				16, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aënea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 5, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pall. Jun. 14, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perforabit aurem ejus subulā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 21, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Deut. 15, 17</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a very small
			weapon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subulā armatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 85, 1</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prov.: subulā leonem excipis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 82, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
